<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbml="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <name>CompositionConcepts</name>
  <type>concept:CompositionConcepts</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MachineBlocks composition and assembly</is>

  <documentation>
    Composition builds larger objects from multiple blocks that share one spatial contract.

    Flat composition places sibling blocks in a shared parent. Nested composition places child
    blocks inside a parent; configuration propagates from parent to children unless overridden.

    A composite wrapper typically hides its own body and studs (base=false, studs=false) and sets
    size to the outer bounding box of its parts. Placement of each part uses direction, offset,
    and alignment relative to the parent origin (alignChildren).

    Assembly modes describe how parts are presented for preview or print: unassembled, assembled,
    or merged. Nested assembly may carry size and direction alongside the mode.

    Calibration at internal contacts often uses a tiny namespaced baseAdjustment overlap so parts
    fuse cleanly when merged. Derived outer size can be computed from part sizes, directions, and
    offsets when no explicit shared size exists.

    In MBOM, composition fills aggregations (for example _parts on CompositeBlock). There is no
    separate Placement meta-block — placement is properties on the placed instances.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="concept:DecisionFramework" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — intent → pattern → parameter decision layers.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:CompositeBlock" relation="Defines">
      Domain type with default _parts aggregation.
    </see>
    <see type="mbml:AuthoringPatterns" relation="SeeAlso">
      MBML composition patterns.
    </see>
    <see type="scad:ModulePatterns" relation="SeeAlso">
      SCAD composite Block File patterns and full-file examples.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
